invested in two Boeing 737 aircraft on lease to two different lessees which also became total losses. In the foregoing examples, the remaining loan balance at the expiration of each respective lease was greater than the fair market value of each
aircraft. In these instances, the aircraft could not have been sold for an amount to satisfy the debt balance and could not be re-leased to a third-party for a lease rate high enough lease to make the debt service payments owed to a lender. As a
