<A NAME="rom80221_102"></A>Taxation of Limited Liability Companies in General </B></FONT></P> <P STYLE="margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:-6px"><FONT SIZE="1">&nbsp;</FONT></P> <P STYLE="margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px; text-indent:4%"><FONT
FACE="Times New Roman" SIZE="2">For income tax purposes, limited liability companies that do not elect to be taxed as corporations are treated as partnerships and, thus, pass through entities. This means that the individual members, and not the
