 <P STYLE="margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px; text-indent:4%"><FONT FACE="Times New Roman" SIZE="2">The economic effect of an allocation is substantial if there is a reasonable possibility that it will
substantially affect the amount to be received by the members from the limited liability company, independent of tax consequences. An economic effect is not substantial if, at the time the allocation becomes part of the LLC Agreement: (1) at least
one member&#146;s after-tax return may, in present value terms, be enhanced compared to his or her return if the allocation were not contained in the LLC Agreement; and (2) there is a strong likelihood that no member&#146;s after-tax return will, in
